Z||000005||BAM-BAM||01-29-2001||10:35 PM||||  Thanks for the idea. But, if I wanted to go that expense and not to mention the effort, I'll just go with the 3800sc SeriesII. 245hp and 275flb torque. Man that sounds nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000006||88formula||01-30-2001||06:28 PM||||Dyno2000 is not optimistic when you use it correctly. I don't use the pull down menus in the program for the heads because they are not accurate. <P>For the stock 2.8-liter engine I got 134 horsepower and 180 ft- lbs. of torque. Those are not optimistic numbers. <P>Using Dragstrip2000 with the above stock engine I get 0-60 mph in 7.96 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.72 @ 86 mph. That seems pretty close to what all the magazines got from a stock 5-speed fiero.<P>Expect to pay more than $1500 for that engine and if you get it for cheaper than your lucky.  I have blueprinted injectors and I’m going to try them first. If guys here can get away with running stock injectors on their 210 horsepower turbocharged 2.8-liter engines than I think I can too. Ed Parks uses stock injectors on his engine but his engine is a stock 3.4 I think. I have the stock ignition system with an upgraded coil. The stock system is actually really good. My throttle body is just polished not bored. The difference in horsepower is about 1-3 peak horsepower, which I think is not worth the $150-dollar expense. I can’t say anything about the chip.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||01-30-2001||08:26 PM||||Bam<BR>You do know that a SC3800 swap will be multi thousand $$||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||01-30-2001||09:10 PM||||  Yes, I am aware of the costs involved in the different swaps. I was courious about the 3.4L power purely to retain the stock appearance and have plenty of power to shut a few people up. Currently my plan is with the 3800sc. If it looks like I might be a little $$ short then the 3.4L HO is a good alternative. Either way, I'll have more than I do now. I think the 3.4L would be a little easier to slip by the smog guys. The time is growing closer and I'm trying to cover my bases as thouroughly as possible. Thanks for all the info and advice. I would appriciate more if possible.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
